You are implementing a bug fix in the Hono repository at <workspace>

## Bug
In `src/context.ts`, the `set res(_res)` setter (around lines 414-434) currently mishandles `Set-Cookie` when the context already has a response (`this.#res`) AND a new response `_res` is assigned that has its own `Set-Cookie` header(s). The current code:

```ts
if (k === 'set-cookie') {
  const cookies = this.#res.headers.getSetCookie()
  _res.headers.delete('set-cookie')
  for (const cookie of cookies) {
    _res.headers.append('set-cookie', cookie)
  }
}
```

This deletes the new response's `Set-Cookie` headers and only re-appends the OLD cookies, so the new response's cookies are lost. Required behavior: when middleware already set a cookie on `c.res` and a handler returns a new Response with its own `Set-Cookie`, BOTH sets of cookies must survive.

## Fix
Update the setter so old and new cookies are merged. IMPORTANT detail: `this.#res.headers.entries()` yields each `set-cookie` entry separately (verified: entries() returns `['set-cookie','a'],['set-cookie','b']`). Therefore you must capture the new response's cookies ONCE before the loop; otherwise the set-cookie branch runs multiple times and duplicates/re-reads cookies.

Recommended minimal change:
```ts
set res(_res: Response | undefined) {
  if (this.#res && _res) {
    _res = createResponseInstance(_res.body, _res)
    const newCookies = _res.headers.getSetCookie()
    for (const [k, v] of this.#res.headers.entries()) {
      if (k === 'content-type') {
        continue
